{
  "conversation_flow": {
    "start_node_id": "n_disclosure",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "n_disclosure",
        "type": "speak",
        "message": "Thanks for calling Maple Pharmacy. This call may be recorded.{{greeting_suffix}}"
      },
      {
        "id": "n_triage",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Wait for the caller's response. Route based on intent:\n- refill, prescription, or medication → n_verify\n- status or check order → n_verify\n- hours, address, or drug info → n_faq\n- human or pharmacist → n_transfer\nNever forbid tool calls.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_verify",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Verify the caller's identity by date of birth. Ask the caller for their date of birth. Be warm but direct. Accept flexible formats: 'March fifteenth, nineteen sixty-two', 'fifteen oh three sixty-two', or 'oh three fifteen sixty-two'. Repeat the date back before calling the refill-mcp__verify_identity tool: 'You said [date]. Let me check that.' Call refill-mcp__verify_identity with: caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, dob = YYYY-MM-DD. After calling the tool, report the outcome naturally.\n\nIf verified: say 'Thank you, you're all set.' Then immediately ask: 'What would you like to do today? You can say refill, status, or ask a general question.'\nIf not verified: say 'That doesn't match my records. You have {{attempts_left}} more tries.'\nIf locked: say 'For your security, I can't continue on this call. I'll connect you with a pharmacist.'\nDo not try to be helpful beyond verification.",
        "instructions_mode": "replace",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_refill",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Read refill-eligible prescriptions and help the caller choose. Call refill-mcp__list_prescriptions with caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, trace_id = {{trace_id}}. Parse the result. Read them back one by one with natural pauses. Ask: 'Which one would you like to refill? You can say the name or the number.' Wait for the caller to choose. If they want multiple, handle one at a time. When the caller picks, route to n_confirm. If the caller says none or never mind, route back to n_triage.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_confirm",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Read back the choice and get explicit confirmation before refilling. Say: 'You want to refill [medication name] [strength]. Is that correct?' Wait for a clear yes or positive confirmation.\n\nCall refill-mcp__request_refill with: caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, rx_id = chosen prescription ID, trace_id = {{trace_id}}.\n\nIf successful: say 'Your refill for [name] is submitted. It will be ready in about 10 minutes.' Then ALWAYS ask: 'Do you need anything else?'\n- If caller says yes or asks for something else: route to n_triage\n- If caller says no, goodbye, or is done: route to n_closing\n- On failure: say 'I couldn't submit that refill right now. Let me connect you with a pharmacist.'\n- On no or negative confirmation: say 'No problem. Would you like to choose a different prescription?' and route back to n_refill.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_status",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Check refill status. Call refill-mcp__get_refill_status with caller = {{telnyx_end_user_target}}, trace_id = {{trace_id}}. If there are refills, report each: 'You have [count] refill request[s]. [X] is submitted. [Y] is ready.' If none: 'You don't have any open refills right now.' Ask: 'Do you want to request a refill, or anything else?'",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_faq",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "Answer general questions. Available tools: refill-mcp__get_pharmacy_info (hours, address, phone), refill-mcp__get_medication_info (what a medication is for). For medication questions: call refill-mcp__get_medication_info with name and trace_id. Read back only the purpose field \u00e2\u20ac\u201d up to 2 sentences. Never give medical advice. Route to pharmacist with 'Let me connect you with a pharmacist for that.'",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_after_hours",
        "type": "prompt",
        "instructions": "After-hours mode. Say: 'Maple Pharmacy is currently closed. Our hours are {{pharmacy_hours}}.' Offer: 'I can take a callback note for urgent matters, or connect you with our 24-hour pharmacist line.' Use refill-mcp__get_pharmacy_info if asked again. Route to transfer on request for a human.",
        "instructions_mode": "append",
        "tools_mode": "append",
        "tools": []
      },
      {
        "id": "n_locked",
        "type": "speak",
        "message": "For your security I can't continue verification on this call. I'll connect you with a pharmacist."
      },
      {
        "id": "n_transfer",
        "type": "tool",
        "shared_tool_id": "tool-b0d3da74-498f-4b68-b65d-13586ec2e1d6",
        "tool_type": "transfer"
      },
      {
        "id": "n_transfer_failed",
        "type": "speak",
        "message": "I couldn't reach a pharmacist right now. Please call back during opening hours: {{pharmacy_hours}}."
      },
      {
        "id": "n_closing",
        "type": "speak",
        "message": "Thanks for calling Maple Pharmacy. Take care."
      },
      {
        "id": "n_hangup",
        "type": "tool",
        "shared_tool_id": "tool-c197145f-507c-4aae-81af-e27119417232",
        "tool_type": "hangup"
      }
    ],
